{title: Goodbye Yesterday}
{artist: Test Worship}
{key: A}
{tempo: 140}
{ccli: 7654321}
{copyright: 2024 Test Music}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[A]Goodbye yesterday
[Asus]I'm living in the light of a new day
[A]I won't waste another minute in my old ways
[A4]Praise the Lord, I've been born again
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Hold G X 8 BARS}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus 1}
[A]Again and again and again and again
[D]You rescued me out of the mess I was in
[A/C#]You traded my sorrow for something to sing
[D]Now I'm dancing on the grave that I once lived in
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[A]Goodbye yesterday
[D]The Spirit of the Lord is upon me
[A/C#]I've got resurrection in my veins
[D]Praise the Lord I've been born
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Interlude}
[A]

{start_of_bridge: Bridge 1}
[A]I have [Bm]decided
[A]To follow [Bm]Jesus
[A]The world be[Bm]hind, the [F#m]cross be[E]fore
[D]And I won't turn back
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus 1}
[A]Again and again and again and again
[D]You rescued me out of the mess I was in
[A/C#]You traded my sorrow for something to sing
[D]Now I'm dancing on the grave that I once lived in
{end_of_chorus}
